UPDATE companies SET description='ASC Auto Electric traces its roots to 1933 in Little Rock, Arkansas, where it began as Armature Service Co. The company has remained in the same city for nine decades, evolving from a local armature repair shop into a national distributor and re-manufacturer of starters and alternators.

Today the business operates as both a distributor and a re-manufacturer, supplying starters, alternators, batteries, custom cables, lighting, turbochargers, fuel injectors and diesel particulate filter cleaning services. Its workshop rebuilds units for everything from ATVs and passenger cars to boats and heavy-duty trucks, while its distribution arm stocks product lines for auto parts retailers across the country and overseas.

Customers include auto parts stores, agricultural equipment dealers, marine service centers and heavy-duty fleet operators. Brands carried range from Briggs & Stratton, Cummins and Kubota engines to Leece-Neville, Denso and Delco Remy electrical components, reflecting a client base that spans agriculture, marine, construction and over-the-road transportation.

The company emphasizes its 85-plus years of experience and a team of technicians who have stayed with the firm for decades. It highlights same-day turnaround on rebuilds — one customer noted a four-hour alternator rebuild at half the cost of a new unit — and a willingness to source hard-to-find OEM parts for individual buyers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Starter and alternator remanufacturing", "Diesel particulate filter (DPF) cleaning", "Custom cable fabrication", "Battery testing and sales", "Lighting system supply", "Turbocharger supply", "Fuel injector supply", "Distribution of auto electrical components", "OEM parts sourcing"], "industries": ["Auto parts retail", "Agriculture", "Marine", "Heavy duty equipment", "Industrial engines"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["85+ years of experience in auto electric parts", "Technicians with decades of tenure", "Alternator rebuilds completed in as little as four hours", "Distributor for leading OEM product lines", "Nationwide and global shipping"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1933 -> /", "Headquarters Little Rock, Arkansas -> db", "Business type: distributor and re-manufacturer of starters and alternators -> /", "Services: starter/alternator rebuilding, DPF cleaning, custom cables, batteries, lighting, turbos, fuel injectors -> /", "Industries served: auto parts stores, agriculture, marine, heavy duty -> /", "Brands carried: Denso, Leece Neville, Delco Remy, Briggs, Cummins, Kubota, etc. -> /", "Testimonial: alternator rebuild in four hours at half cost -> /", "Team with decades of tenure -> /", "Nationwide and global distribution -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "distributor and re-manufacturer of starters and alternators", "founded_year": "1933", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": 