UPDATE companies SET description='Accu-Mold Plastics is headquartered in Halifax, Pennsylvania. The company was founded in 1972 by Jack L. Strohecker and his wife Mary Lou, who began the business as a tool and die operation in the basement of their home. Initially focused on precision mold building for the electronics industry, the company quickly earned a reputation for craftsmanship that attracted early clients such as American Catheter Company and Hamilton Watch.

Today Accu-Mold operates a 9,000‑square‑foot facility that was rebuilt after an F‑1 tornado destroyed the original plant in 2006. The shop houses automated injection molding machines ranging from 22 to 125 tons of clamping force, with shot capacities from 1.2 to just under 9 ounces. In‑house capabilities include mold design using SOLIDWORKS, Mastercam and AutoCAD, CNC machining, sinker EDM, surface grinding, manual machining and heat treating. A geothermal‑controlled clean room supports medical‑grade production, and the company offers overmolding, insert molding, assembly, packaging and just‑in‑time delivery.

The company serves the electronics and medical device sectors, with a historical focus on medical disposables. Its customer base includes both established manufacturers and start‑ups that rely on Accu‑Mold’s ability to move from single‑cavity prototypes to full‑scale production runs.

Accu‑Mold emphasizes efficiency, competitive pricing and responsive customer support as its core differentiators. By integrating the latest molding technologies with streamlined processes, the company aims to deliver high‑quality, precision components that help customers stay competitive, whether they need low‑volume prototypes or large production quantities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision injection molding", "Mold design and engineering", "In\u2011house mold building", "CNC machining", "Sinker EDM", "Surface grinding", "Manual machining", "Heat treating", "Overmolding", "Insert molding", "Part assembly", "Packaging", "Just\u2011in\u2011time delivery", "Clean room molding", "Prototyping", "Full\u2011scale production", "Service and repairs"], "industries": ["Electronics", "Medical devices", "Medical disposables"], "materials": ["Plastics"], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (22\u2013125 tons)", "CNC machines", "Sinker EDM", "Surface grinders", "Manual machining equipment", "Heat treating furnaces", "Geothermal\u2011controlled clean room"], "volume": "Prototype to full\u2011scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Complete in\u2011house mold design, tooling and injection molding under one roof", "Geothermal\u2011controlled clean room for medical\u2011grade production", "Overmolding and insert molding capabilities", "Rapid recovery capability \u2013 operations resumed within eight days after a tornado", "Decades\u2011long employee retention (e.g., 40\u2011year anniversary noted)"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Halifax, PA -> db", "Founded 1972 by Jack L. Strohecker and Mary Lou -> /about", "Started as tool and die in basement -> /about", "Early clients: American Catheter Company, Hamilton Watch -> /about", "9,000 sq ft facility built 1985, rebuilt after 2006 tornado -> /about", "Injection molding machines 22\u2013125 tons, shot sizes 1.2\u20139 oz -> /services", "In\u2011house mold design with SOLIDWORKS, Mastercam, AutoCAD -> /services", "CNC machining, sinker EDM, surface grinding, manual machining, heat treating -> /services", "Clean room, overmolding, insert molding, assembly, packaging, JIT delivery -> /services", "Industries: electronics, medical disposables -> /about, /services", "ISO\u2011Certified Medical Molding claim -> /", "Employee Lee Bechtel 40\u2011year anniversary -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Accu-Mold Plastics is a trusted, full-service provider of precision injection-molded plastic components", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='accu-mold-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Luvata Waterbury operates in Waterbury, Connecticut, tracing its roots to the 1971 founding of Intermagnetics General Corporation (IGC). The business was acquired by Outokumpu Copper Products Oy in 2001 and rebranded under the Luvata name in 2006. Since 2017 it has been a subsidiary of Mitsubishi Materials Corporation.

The facility manufactures copper-stabilized niobium-titanium (NbTi) and niobium-tin (Nb3Sn) conductors, producing low-temperature superconducting wire and cable for applications where delivery and performance are critical. A team of over 100 professionals supports production for medical diagnostic systems such as MRI, as well as high-energy physics projects.

The company’s superconductors have been selected for major international projects including the Large Hadron Collider at CERN, the KSTAR fusion research device in Korea, and the ITER experimental reactor. It has also fulfilled a $26 million nuclear fusion contract for the U.S. Department of Energy and a $6.5 million supply agreement for CEA Saclay.

