UPDATE companies SET description='Acue-Tex Inc is a family-owned injection molding company based in Hubbard, Oregon, a short drive south of Portland on I-5. The business was started in 1987 by Michael and Glorianna Terrell, who initially operated from a small shop near their home before building the current 6,000-square-foot facility in the early 1990s. Michael Terrell continues to run the in-house tool and die shop, drawing on more than 40 years in the plastics industry.

The company operates 13 injection molding machines with clamp forces ranging from 20 to 300 tons, focusing on small to medium-sized plastic parts. Six of those machines are vertical presses dedicated to insert molding, producing over two million insert-molded components each year—items such as hubs on cannulae, obturators, plastic tubing, and steel pins. Acue-Tex also maintains an in-house tool and die shop that builds the majority of the tooling running on its floor, allowing for on-site repairs and maintenance with short lead times. The team of 14 employees handles plastic fabrication, tool building, and molding operations.

The bulk of the customer base serves the medical, dental, and veterinary markets, which requires stringent quality control systems and full process control and traceability throughout manufacturing. The company works with materials including ABS, polystyrene, and polyethylene, and reuses over 6,000 pounds of its own scrap ABS annually; in 2018 it processed more than 84,000 pounds of recycled polystyrene and polyethylene, making recycled content nearly 40 percent of material input.

Acue-Tex distinguishes itself through honesty, transparency, and a personal commitment to getting things right, whether starting a project from scratch, building tools, or refurbishing existing programs. The ownership emphasizes reliability and knowledge at every step, aiming to exceed expectations on both cost and quality.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Insert Molding", "Tool and Die Manufacturing", "Plastic Fabrication"], "industries": ["Medical", "Dental", "Veterinary"], "materials": ["ABS", "Polystyrene", "Polyethylene", "Recycled plastics"], "equipment": ["13 injection molding machines (20-300 ton clamp)", "6 vertical molding machines for insert molding"], "volume": "Over 2 million insert molded components annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tool and die shop builds and repairs most tooling", "Six dedicated vertical molding machines for insert molding", "Processes over 2 million insert molded components annually", "Recycles over 6,000 lbs of scrap ABS per year", "Full process control and traceability for medical, dental, veterinary markets"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1987 by Michael and Glorianna Terrell -> /", "Family-owned small business -> /", "Headquarters in Hubbard, Oregon -> /", "6,000 sq ft facility built in early 1990s -> /", "13 injection molding machines (20-300 ton clamp) -> /", "6 vertical molding machines for insert molding -> /", "Over 2 million insert molded components annually -> /", "In-house tool and die shop builds majority of tooling -> /", "Team of 14 employees -> /", "Serves medical, dental, veterinary markets -> /", "Stringent quality control, full process control and traceability -> /", "Reuses over 6,000 lbs scrap ABS annually -> /", "Processed 84,000 lbs recycled polystyrene and polyethylene in 2018 -> /", "Differentiators: honesty, transparency, personal commitment -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a small, family owned injection molding company with over 40 years of experience.", "founded_year": "1987", "employee_count": "14", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='acue-tex-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Acuity Medical Inc was founded in 1987 in Annapolis, Maryland. The company operates as a medical device manufacturer, specialty distributor, and contract sales agency.

The company maintains a warehouse, customer service department, and logistics infrastructure to distribute and wholesale medical products. Its service offerings include equipment installation, clinical in-services, IDN pricing contracts with staging and assembly, consulting and sales support, and white-glove delivery. Acuity also runs marketing programs that combine face-to-face presentations, e-marketing, telemarketing, and trade-show representation for its manufacturer partners.

Acuity serves the healthcare continuum, targeting hospitals, alternate-care facilities, home medical equipment (HME/DME) providers, and medical/surgical distributors. Its sales team covers the United States with regional representatives, and the company works with medical device manufacturers as a contract sales agency to grow revenue through its Partner Focus Program.

